{
  "workflowId": "300000331058418",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_TIME_AND_LABOR_FAST_FORMULA_AGENT",
  "name": "Time and Labor Fast Formula Agent",
  "description": "Agent team for Time and Labor fast formula generation.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Initial Conversation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "set_intake_variables"
          },
          "code": "INITIAL_CONVERSATION",
          "id": "1",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the intake extraction node for Oracle HCM Time and Labor Fast Formula requests.\n\nUse these runtime values:\n\nORIGINAL_REQUEST:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nCURRENT_USER_MESSAGE:\n{{$context.$nodes.APPROVAL.$feedbackReceived||$context.$nodes.APPROVAL.$feedbackRecieved||$context.$nodes.REQUEST_MISSING_DETAILS.$feedbackReceived||$context.$nodes.REQUEST_MISSING_DETAILS.$feedbackRecieved||$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nLAST_FAST_FORMULA_TYPE:\n{{$context.$variables.intakeFastFormulaType}}\n\nLAST_REQUIREMENTS:\n{{$context.$variables.intakeRequirements}}\n\nLAST_INPUTS:\n{{$context.$variables.intakeInputs}}\n\nLAST_OUTPUTS:\n{{$context.$variables.intakeOutputs}}\n\nReturn valid JSON only. Do not return markdown, prose, labels outside JSON, code, pseudocode, or file content.\n\nRequired JSON shape:\n{\n  \"FastFormulaType\": \"<value>\",\n  \"requirements\": \"<value>\",\n  \"inputs\": \"<value>\",\n  \"outputs\": \"<value>\"\n}\n\nDecision priority:\n1. Evaluate CURRENT_USER_MESSAGE as the active message.\n2. If CURRENT_USER_MESSAGE contains labeled corrections, update only those fields and preserve every other LAST_* value. Treat singular/plural input and output labels as the same fields.\n3. If CURRENT_USER_MESSAGE is a simple confirmation such as yes, approved, correct, ok, proceed, go ahead, or looks good, preserve all LAST_* values.\n4. If CURRENT_USER_MESSAGE is rejection-only, such as no, incorrect, wrong, or not right, and gives no replacement details, preserve LAST_* values but use Unknown - confirm for any missing FastFormulaType, inputs, or outputs.\n5. Otherwise extract intake details from CURRENT_USER_MESSAGE, using ORIGINAL_REQUEST only as background context.\n\nCorrection labels to recognize, with either - or : after the label:\n- Fast Formula Type\n- Formula Type\n- Requirements\n- Input\n- Inputs\n- Required Inputs\n- Output\n- Outputs\n- Expected Outputs\n\nFor unlabeled intake extraction:\nOutput contract (strict, highest priority)\nYou must produce a requirements summary only for an Oracle HCM Time and Labor formula.\nDo not generate Fast Formula code, pseudocode, file content, or create/modify files.\nBe concise. Include only details that are directly relevant to the stated requirement.\n\nProhibited actions\nNo Fast Formula syntax (DEFAULT FOR, INPUTS ARE, RETURN, loops, etc.)\nNo code blocks containing formula logic\nNo file creation (e.g., .ff) or patching\nNo implementation-level script/output\nIf the user asks for code, explain that this prompt is summary-only and provide the summary format below.\n\nRequired response format\nRequired Inputs\nInclude only explicit rule parameters that must be configured by the implementer\nDo not include data supplied automatically by the Time and Labor engine\nOmit standard or optional parameters unless they materially affect the requested behavior\nWhen the requirement includes configurable business values such as thresholds, time bands, limits, or message text, present them as rule parameters instead of hard-coded values\nDBIs / Runtime Context\nInclude relevant data provided by DBIs, formula context, or the Time and Labor engine\nInclude only context that is necessary to explain how the requirement will be evaluated\nExpected Outputs\nInclude only outputs directly produced by this requirement\nOmit unused buckets, audit outputs, or generic template outputs\nBusiness Goal\nSummarize the requested behavior in plain language\nOpen Questions\nInclude this section only if essential information is missing\nAsk only questions that are necessary to correctly define the requested formula behavior\nDo not include generic or speculative questions\nQuality gate before responding\nCheck all:\n\n No code or pseudocode included\n No file generation/editing implied\n Only requirement-relevant inputs and outputs included\n Engine-provided data is listed under DBIs / Runtime Context, not Required Inputs\n Configurable business values are presented as rule parameters when relevant\n Open Questions included only when essential and directly relevant\n\nFast Formula Type mapping:\n- time calculation rule, calculation rule, time calculation, overtime, premium pay, premium entries, hours over threshold -> Time Calculation Rules\n- time entry rule, entry rule, time entry, validating time card entries, messages, errors, warnings -> Time Entry Rules\n- time device rule, device rule, time device, clock events, device exceptions -> Time Device Rules\n- time submission rule, submission rule, time submission, auto save, auto submit -> Time Submission Rules\n- time compliance rule, compliance rule, time compliance, workforce compliance, regulatory or policy noncompliance -> Time Compliance Rules\n\nIf multiple Fast Formula Type mappings match or no mapping matches, use Unknown - confirm unless LAST_FAST_FORMULA_TYPE already has a known allowed value.\n\nFinal check before returning JSON:\n- Preserve prior values for fields not corrected.\n- If only inputs are corrected, the next approval message must show the corrected inputs while preserving the prior Fast Formula Type, requirements, and outputs.\n- Do not invent missing business details.\n- Do not generate Fast Formula code.\n- Return only the JSON object."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"outputs\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"inputs\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"requirements\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"FastFormulaType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"FastFormulaType\",\n    \"inputs\",\n    \"outputs\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Intake Variables"
